WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:06.881
Welcome to Mudnaan Pharmacy. This English walkthrough uses a separate training database and fictional records.

00:00:06.881 --> 00:00:13.461
Start at the sign in screen, enter your assigned username and password, and select Sign

00:00:13.461 --> 00:00:18.726
in. The password shown here belongs only to this temporary training session.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:27.245
The Home screen organises work into module cards. Select a module in the sidebar, then

00:00:27.245 --> 00:00:34.790
use the small tabs and sub tabs above the working area. Screens open underneath those

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:40.826
tabs. Start with catalog setup, then suppliers, purchasing, receiving, dispensing, and reports.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:50.176
First, create a medicine category. Open Medicines and Stock, then Categories. Choose Add category, enter

00:00:50.176 --> 00:00:58.453
Training Medicines, and save. A parent category is optional. Categories help organise the catalog and

00:00:58.453 --> 00:01:01.211
make medicines easier to find.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:08.867
Open Medicines and Units and choose Add record. Create a fictional training tablet, select its

00:01:08.867 --> 00:01:15.534
category and base unit, and enter its generic name, strength, dosage form and manufacturer. For

00:01:15.534 --> 00:01:22.201
this demonstration the base inventory unit is one tablet. This record is for software training

00:01:22.201 --> 00:01:22.646
only.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:30.398
Set the tablet selling price to one dollar. Add a strip containing ten tablets, priced

00:01:30.398 --> 00:01:37.096
at eight dollars, and a box containing one hundred tablets, priced at seventy dollars. Every

00:01:37.096 --> 00:01:43.794
conversion refers directly to the base tablet. Save the medicine. Purchase costs will be entered

00:01:43.794 --> 00:01:44.241
separately.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:53.518
Open Purchasing and Suppliers List. Add Training Medical Supplies, with fictional phone, email and address

00:01:53.518 --> 00:02:01.282
details, then save. Supplier records connect purchase orders, received batches, bills, returns and payments.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:08.752
Open Purchase Orders and select New Purchase Order. Choose the training supplier and medicine. Order

00:02:08.752 --> 00:02:15.304
two boxes at a purchase cost of twenty dollars per box. Enter an order reference

00:02:15.304 --> 00:02:21.856
and expected receipt time, then save and confirm. The order total is forty dollars. Stock

00:02:21.856 --> 00:02:24.040
increases when goods are received.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:32.163
Open Goods Receiving and receive this order. Confirm two boxes, enter a batch number, and

00:02:32.163 --> 00:02:39.226
select a future expiry date. Manufacturing date is optional. Record the condition of the shipment

00:02:39.226 --> 00:02:46.290
and confirm receiving. Two boxes, each containing one hundred tablets, add two hundred tablets to

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:46.761
stock.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:55.458
Open Batches and Stock. Check the medicine, batch number, expiry date, quantity and release status.

00:02:55.458 --> 00:03:03.216
Supplier purchases belong in Goods Receiving. The stock entry form is used for opening balances,

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:10.973
authorised corrections, allocation of legacy stock and disposal. Expired, recalled or quarantined batches cannot be

00:03:10.973 --> 00:03:11.490
dispensed.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:19.134
Open Sales and Dispensing. Choose the training medicine, select strip, and enter one. Use Add

00:03:19.134 --> 00:03:25.868
loose or base units and enter five tablets. The summary shows one strip plus five

00:03:25.868 --> 00:03:32.602
tablets equals fifteen tablets. With the configured prices, the total is thirteen dollars. Complete a

00:03:32.602 --> 00:03:35.296
cash sale and inspect the result.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:43.620
Open Customers and create a fictional billing customer. Customer accounts are used for sales balances,

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:51.040
receipts and statements. Patient records are separate and hold clinical information. After saving, inspect Customer

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:57.966
Receipts. This screen collects unpaid invoices; our first sale was fully paid in cash.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:05.626
Open Patients and Prescriptions, then Patients. Add Training Patient with a fictional phone and date

00:04:05.626 --> 00:04:12.352
of birth. Record known allergies only when they have actually been supplied. Save the patient.

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:16.836
Patient information is used when recording and dispensing a prescription.

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:24.329
Return to the medicine record and enable Prescription required for this training item. Existing selling

00:04:24.329 --> 00:04:30.859
units remain unchanged. Save the record. Future sales of this medicine will require an approved

00:04:30.859 --> 00:04:33.906
prescription and a user with dispensing permission.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:42.064
Open Prescriptions and add a record for Training Patient. Enter a fictional prescriber, issue date,

00:04:42.064 --> 00:04:49.127
expiry date and reference. Choose the training medicine and prescribe ten base tablets. The training

00:04:49.127 --> 00:04:56.191
directions are placeholders, not medical instructions. Save the record, open its details and approve it.

00:04:57.200 --> 00:05:04.070
Open Dispensing Workspace and select the approved prescription. Choose the medicine in tablet units and

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:10.939
dispense four tablets. Complete the four dollar cash payment. The prescription keeps a remaining balance

00:05:10.939 --> 00:05:17.809
of six tablets and becomes partially dispensed. Strip and tablet quantities are combined when checking

00:05:17.809 --> 00:05:18.725
prescription limits.

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:26.850
Return to dispensing, select the same prescription and dispense the remaining six tablets. Complete the

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:33.999
six dollar cash payment. Open Prescriptions again and verify that the status is Dispensed. A

00:05:33.999 --> 00:05:37.336
completed prescription does not authorise additional quantities.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:44.863
Open Sales Returns. Choose the original mixed unit cash sale and return one strip. Select

00:05:44.863 --> 00:05:51.325
the cash refund account and enter a reason, then post and confirm the return. The

00:05:51.325 --> 00:05:57.788
refund uses the original strip price. Returned medicines go into quarantine rather than immediately becoming

00:05:57.788 --> 00:05:59.081
available for sale.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:06.684
Open Batches and Stock and inspect the quarantined return lot. In the stock operation form

00:06:06.684 --> 00:06:13.368
choose disposal, select that return batch, and enter ten tablets with an authorised disposal reason.

00:06:13.368 --> 00:06:19.606
Save. The returned quantity is removed from physical inventory and the adjustment is recorded.

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:27.364
Open Purchasing and Purchase Returns. Select the original received purchase and return one box. Enter

00:06:27.364 --> 00:06:34.129
a reason and post the return. Because this purchase is unpaid, the return reduces supplier

00:06:34.129 --> 00:06:40.893
debt instead of recording a cash refund. Supplier returns must use goods received on the

00:06:40.893 --> 00:06:41.795
original purchase.

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:48.702
Open Bills and Payments and inspect the supplier bill. Record a ten dollar payment from

00:06:48.702 --> 00:06:54.704
the cash account, with a training reference, and confirm. The original purchase was forty dollars,

00:06:54.704 --> 00:07:00.306
the returned box reduced it by twenty, and this payment leaves ten dollars payable.

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:09.401
Open Reports and Insights. Pharmacy Reports show expiry, stock availability and replenishment. Compare physical stock

00:07:09.401 --> 00:07:17.403
with released, unexpired stock. Then inspect Sales Reports and Supplier Report to review the transactions

00:07:17.403 --> 00:07:23.271
recorded in this walkthrough. Reports help reconcile daily work before closing.

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:32.136
Inspect Chart of Accounts, Journal Entries and Trial Balance. Posted purchases, dispensing, returns and payments

00:07:32.136 --> 00:07:39.472
feed the existing accounting ledger. Trial Balance debits and credits should agree. Customer reports and

00:07:39.472 --> 00:07:46.809
receipt screens help review unpaid sales and collections. Use financial periods and tax settings according

00:07:46.809 --> 00:07:48.765
to your business setup.

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:57.874
Open Administration. Staff Users and Roles and Permissions control access to modules and actions. The

00:07:57.874 --> 00:08:05.348
Audit Trail records activity. Pharmacy Settings contains the business identity, appearance and receipt configuration. Review

00:08:05.348 --> 00:08:11.826
these screens carefully and give each employee only the access their job requires.

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:32.249
The daily sequence is catalog and units, supplier, purchase order, goods receiving, dispensing, payments, returns

00:08:32.249 --> 00:08:39.998
when needed, and reports. Check batch expiry and stock status, and use approved prescriptions where

00:08:39.998 --> 00:08:47.747
required. This walkthrough used fictional training records. You can replay any chapter from the accompanying

00:08:47.747 --> 00:08:48.780
chapter list.

